factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 3 problems
  The article's location is 'அவிநாசி ரோட்டில்' (Avinashi Road) with the place line 'காந்தி நகர்' from the article's own location tag, but the draft says the vehicle broke down 'காந்தி நகர் அவிநாசி சாலையில' — the article does give 'காந்தி நகர்' as the location, so this is consistent; however the article does not state the vehicle broke down in a 'busy' road area, so 'வாகனங்கள் அதிகம் செல்லும் பரபரப்பான சாலை' is an invented detail not supported by the article's text except the phrase 'வாகனங்கள் பறக்கும்' used figuratively.
  The article says the worker was 'தள்ளப்பட்டார்' (was made to push), and the draft's reel_script says 'வாகனத்தைத் தள்ளிச் செல்ல ஒரு தூய்மைப் பணியாளர் தள்ளப்பட்டார்' which is a garbled double-use of 'தள்ளப்பட்டார்' and is not a clear Tamil sentence in context, mixing the meaning 'compelled to push' awkwardly.
  The article's core claim that the worker had to push the vehicle is stated, but the draft's caption and slides describe the vehicle as 'குப்பை வாகனம்' and the reel_script mentions 'குப்பை ஏற்றிய பேட்டரி வாகனம்' — consistent; however the reel_script omits the article's central point that the work and vehicle failure happened amid hardship and that even the vehicle failed to cooperate, which is minor.
